{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observed signal\nError sweep window 2026-08-30T21:20:00-07:00..2026-09-01T11:58:00-07:00 (2026-08-31T04:20:00Z..2026-09-01T18:58:00Z) found GitHub Actions run 33455923923 (`Jira DC Exact-Patchset Parity`, workflow_dispatch, triggered by JoeOakhartNava) failed before executing the live DC parity body.\n\nFailing job: `jira DC exact-patchset parity (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)` at step `Verify the checkout landed on the exact patchset SHA`.\n\nError:\n`checked-out HEAD (d6c37680805fc8ae013832dd4c09c1fb100a1e0b) does not match the requested Gerrit patchset revision (a22257e7d10e3d079ee676cbb38d2b39811d0fd5) — refusing to run the DC lane against the wrong ref.`\n\n## Confirmed root cause\nGerrit change 2466 patchset 1 (`refs/changes/66/2466/1`) resolves to `d6c37680805fc8ae013832dd4c09c1fb100a1e0b`; patchset 2/current resolves to `a22257e7d10e3d079ee676cbb38d2b39811d0fd5`. Run 33455923923 combined the patchset-1 refspec with the patchset-2 revision. The pinned `checkout-gerrit-change-action` first checks out its `ref` default (`github.sha`) but then fetches `GERRIT_REFSPEC` and unconditionally checks out `FETCH_HEAD`, so the workflow landed on the stale refspec commit and only the later guard detected the mismatch.\n\nThe guard's fail-closed behavior is correct. The defect is that `.github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml` delegates the exact checkout to a refspec-first third-party action and does not validate `FETCH_HEAD == GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION` before selecting the final checkout commit.\n\n## Fix plan\nReplace the third-party checkout step in `.github/workflows/jira-dc-exact-patchset.yml` with explicit shell plumbing that:\n\n1. initializes a git repository in the runner workspace;\n2. fetches the exact `GERRIT_REFSPEC` from the GitHub mirror, with Gerrit as a fallback;\n3. fails with a clear fetch error if neither source can fetch the requested refspec;\n4. compares `FETCH_HEAD^{commit}` to `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION` and fails with a clear input-mismatch error if they differ;\n5. checks out `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION` explicitly and verifies `git rev-parse HEAD` equals it before any Python/Jira DC setup or live DC operation runs.\n\nStrengthen `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py` so it executes the checkout shell from the workflow against temporary git remotes. The RED oracle is an inconsistent input pair (refspec points at one commit, `GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION` names another) that currently exits only after the third-party action has checked out the wrong ref; the fixed workflow must fail at the fetch/input validation seam with no different HEAD selected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The Jira DC exact-patchset parity workflow checks out the exact requested Gerrit patchset SHA before any live DC operation runs; checked by `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py -q` and by the existing `HEAD == GERRIT_PATCHSET_REVISION` guard embedded in the workflow.\n- [ ] If the requested patchset refspec cannot be fetched from either the GitHub mirror or Gerrit fallback, the workflow fails with a clear fetch/input error rather than landing on a different commit; checked by a focused temporary-git test in `tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py`.\n- [ ] A rerun or equivalent dispatch for the affected patchset reaches the DC parity checks with `HEAD == expected_sha`.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions workflow_dispatch with real Jira Data Center image; principal=Gerrit/GitHub workflow actor; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — the real Jira DC Docker image only runs in CI, so this session proves the checkout/verify plumbing locally and relies on Gerrit `Verified` plus a future explicit dispatch for the live DC body.\n\n## Testing\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_jira_dc_exact_patchset_workflow.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test`\n\nDo not run the real Jira DC parity body locally; the operator confirmed the real Data Center Docker image used by this lane only runs in CI."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788314860301056488,"uuid":"192abece-e8a7-4b2d-adc9-1699d320a629"}